    [BugFix] Backport ViT mRoPE 16-token blocks to v0.32.0rc (#20445)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Backport #19129 onto `releases/v0.32.0rc`, starting from
    ffca1c99bb28d9c92dd5dcf327f8b242404a5055. Reapply commits 9e0488b and
    9bfa732 with the release branch's worker import structure and ordering
    preserved.
    
    Fix the MiniMax-M3 ViT mRoPE UB capacity compilation failure on Ascend
    A5 by using 16-token blocks for the launch grid and BLOCK_N, reusing the
    upstream Triton kernel unchanged. Preserve metadata, output
    layout/dtype, BLOCK_D and num_warps=8. Replace the legacy function and
    its already-loaded MiniMax vision-tower alias during worker
    initialization, before model construction; later imports receive the
    patched function.
    
    This temporary patch targets the legacy-function interface. After
    upgrading to the pluggable VitMropeSetup interface from
    vllm-project/vllm#63017, replace it with Ascend registration and remove
    the patch.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Fixes the reported MiniMax-M3 startup failure on Ascend A5 with the
    legacy-function interface. No new configuration or environment
    variables. Release note: `release_notes/fragments/20445.yaml` (YAML
    parsing passed).
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `py -3.12 tests/ut/patch/worker/test_patch_mrope_vit_setup.py`: passed
    on the release-based branch; covers block boundaries and preloaded model
    aliases, launch parameters, metadata, output shape and unchanged kernel
    identity.
    - Ruff lint and format checks passed for the patch and both test files.
    - `git diff origin/releases/v0.32.0rc --check`: passed.
    - Model accuracy validation completed: TextVQA score **72.4805**.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
